-### Ray Packet BVH Traversal
-Processes multiple rays simultaneously for SIMD efficiency. Choose for GPU or SIMD-heavy CPU implementations. [Link](21088-ray-packet-bvh-traversal.md)
+**Edge Cases:**
+*   Ray parallel to triangle: `det` near zero.
+*   Ray origin inside triangle: handled by $t > \epsilon$ check.
+*   Degenerate triangles: `det` near zero.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \log M)$ on average, where $N$ is the number of rays and $M$ is the number of triangles. Worst case $O(N \cdot M)$ for degenerate BVHs.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(M)$ for the BVH structure.
-*   **Performance:** Pure ray tracing achieves ~1.1 billion primary rays/s and ~1.3 billion rays/s with shadows/AO on RTX 3080 Ti [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Exact intersections, sharp CSG support, no marching errors.
-*   **Limitations:** Slower than sphere tracing for smooth SDFs, sensitive to BVH quality.
-*   **When to use:** When exact geometry is required, or for shadow rays.
-*   **When not to use:** For smooth SDFs where sphere tracing is faster, or for very large scenes with poor BVH construction.
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \log M)$ average case for $N$ rays and $M$ triangles, dependent on BVH quality [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(M)$ for BVH storage [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** ~1.1 billion primary rays/s and ~1.3 billion rays/s with shadows/AO on RTX 3080 Ti [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Exact for sharp CSG, no distance function needed, efficient pruning [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Slower than sphere tracing for smooth shapes, requires BVH construction [S1, unofficial].
+*   **When to use:** Sharp geometry, CSG operations, shadow rays [S1, unofficial].
+*   **When not to use:** Smooth organic shapes, real-time sphere tracing preferred [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Originated from the need for exact ray-triangle intersection in software ray tracers. The method is described in the context of "EBGeometry" and "Visualization: sphere-traced rendering of shapes and tapes" [S1, unofficial]. It is used in interactive viewers for sharp CSG rendering.
+Originated in the context of sphere-traced rendering of shapes and tapes, specifically for "Pure ray tracing" mode in EBGeometry [S1, unofficial]. It leverages existing packed BVHs for mesh SDFs, avoiding new acceleration structure construction [S1, unofficial]. Used in interactive viewers for sharp CSG scenes like the "Tunnel" and "Rod" examples [S1, unofficial].
 
